<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Guelph Community Gardens &mdash; Reference Layer for OSM Editors</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="index.css">
<link rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css"
      integrity="sha256-p4NxAoJBhIIN+hmNHrzRCf9tD/miZyoHS5obTRR9BMY="
      crossorigin="">
<script defer src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js"
        integrity="sha256-20nQCchB9co0qIjJZRGuk2/Z9VM+kNiyxNV1lvTlZBo="
        crossorigin=""></script>
<script defer src="index.js"></script>
<script data-goatcounter="https://osm-guelph.goatcounter.com/count" async src="//gc.zgo.at/count.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
<main>

<h1>Guelph Community Gardens</h1>
<p class="lead">
  A reference layer of the community gardens on the City of Guelph's roster
  &mdash; <strong>{{FOOD_COUNT}}</strong> food-growing gardens and
  <strong>{{POLLINATOR_COUNT}}</strong> pollinator patches, with the City's
  outline wherever it has drawn one &mdash; ready to add to the
  <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org">OpenStreetMap</a> editors
  <strong>iD</strong> and <strong>JOSM</strong> while you map.
</p>
<p class="meta">City roster: {{POINTS_DATE}} &middot; City footprints: {{POLYGONS_DATE}} &middot; tiles rebuilt: {{BUILD_DATE}}</p>

<div class="attribution">
  <a href="{{LICENSE_URL}}">{{LICENSE_NOTICE}}</a>
  Sources: <a href="{{POINTS_PAGE}}">Community Gardens</a> and
  <a href="{{POLYGONS_PAGE}}">Community Gardens Polygons</a>.
</div>

<h2>Preview</h2>
<div id="preview-map" data-raster-url="{{RASTER_URL}}"></div>
<p class="meta">
  The raster layer drawn over OpenStreetMap. Green outlines are the City's
  garden footprints; a green dot marks a food garden too small to see at this
  zoom or with no footprint at all; amber dots are pollinator patches.
</p>

<div class="attribution">
  <strong>Coverage vs OpenStreetMap:</strong> see which City gardens are
  <a href="gaps/">missing from OSM, untagged, unnamed or named differently</a>
  &mdash; a mapper's worklist with an interactive map and table.
</div>

<h2>Two layers &mdash; which to use</h2>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th>Vector layer</th>
    <td>Interactive. Click a garden to read its tags (<code>name</code>,
        <code>city_name</code>, <code>type</code>, <code>kind</code>,
        <code>address</code>, <code>footprint</code>, <code>garden_id</code>).
        Best in <strong>iD</strong>.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <th>Raster layer</th>
    <td>Outlines, dots and names drawn directly on the tiles. A readable
        backdrop. Best in <strong>JOSM</strong>.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<div class="note">
  <strong>Treat the outline as a hint, not a trace.</strong> Many of the City's
  footprints are a single bed &mdash; the median is about 230&nbsp;m&sup2;
  &mdash; and the footprint layer has not been redrawn since mid-2025. Map
  what is on the ground or in current imagery, usually
  <code>leisure=garden</code> + <code>garden:type=community</code> around the
  whole plot area.
</div>

<h2>Add to iD</h2>
<h3>Vector layer (interactive)</h3>
<ol>
  <li>Open the iD editor and press <kbd>U</kbd> for the <em>Map Data</em> panel.</li>
  <li>Under <em>Custom Map Data</em>, open the settings and paste this URL:</li>
</ol>
<pre class="url">{{VECTOR_URL}}</pre>
<p>Zoom in, then click any garden to see its tags in the inspector.</p>

<h3>Raster layer (visible names)</h3>
<ol>
  <li>Open the <em>Background</em> panel and choose <em>Custom</em>.</li>
  <li>Paste this URL template:</li>
</ol>
<pre class="url">{{RASTER_URL}}</pre>

<h2>Add to JOSM</h2>
<h3>Raster layer (recommended for JOSM)</h3>
<ol>
  <li>Open <em>Preferences &rarr; Imagery</em> and click <strong>+TMS</strong>.</li>
  <li>Paste this entry (the <code>tms[13,17]</code> prefix sets the zoom range;
      JOSM scales it up past z17):</li>
</ol>
<pre class="url">tms[13,17]:{{RASTER_URL_JOSM}}</pre>
<p>
  Give it a name such as <em>Guelph Community Gardens</em>, click OK, then
  enable it from the <em>Imagery</em> menu. Note JOSM's placeholder is
  <code>{zoom}</code>, not <code>{z}</code>.
</p>

<h3>Vector layer (optional)</h3>
<p>
  JOSM can also add the vector tiles via <em>Preferences &rarr; Imagery</em> &rarr;
  <strong>+MVT</strong>:
</p>
<pre class="url">{{VECTOR_URL_JOSM}}</pre>

<h2>Notes</h2>
<ul>
  <li>The City's point layer is the <strong>roster</strong>: it decides which
      gardens exist and what they are called. It is kept current (two gardens
      added in June 2026). The polygon layer only lends a garden its outline,
      joined on the City's garden id; the three newest gardens have none and
      are drawn as a dot.</li>
  <li>Gardens the City marks as future are left out.</li>
  <li>Names are the City's ALL CAPS roster names, title-cased for the map
      (<code>city_name</code> keeps them verbatim). Check the sign before
      copying one.</li>
  <li><strong>Pollinator patches</strong> are drawn but kept apart: OSM has no
      settled tag for a pollinator garden, and the gap page does not count them.</li>
  <li>Vector tiles are pre-rendered for zooms 12&ndash;19; raster tiles for
      z13&ndash;17 (the editor overzooms them further).</li>
  <li>Tiles are refreshed weekly from the City's service.</li>
  <li>This is a <strong>reference</strong> layer &mdash; verify against survey or
      imagery before copying anything into OpenStreetMap.</li>
</ul>

